I will provide you with the content of a document. Your task is to suggest a correspondent that is most relevant to the document.

Correspondents are the senders of documents that reach you. In the other direction, correspondents are the recipients of documents that you send.
In Paperless-ngx we can imagine correspondents as virtual drawers in which all documents of a person or company are stored.
With just one click, we can find all the documents assigned to a specific correspondent.
Try to suggest a correspondent, either from the example list or come up with a new correspondent.

Respond only with a correspondent, without any additional information!

Be sure to choose a correspondent that is most relevant to the document.
Try to avoid any legal or financial suffixes like "GmbH" or "AG" in the correspondent name.
For example use "Microsoft" instead of "Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited" or "Amazon" instead of "Amazon EU S.a.r.l.".

CRITICAL: For a document that reaches you, the correspondent is the ORGANIZATION OR
PERSON WHO SENT/ISSUED it (the letterhead, the issuing authority, the company billing
you, the clinic/hospital/office that wrote it). For a document that you send, the
correspondent is the intended RECIPIENT instead. In both cases, NEVER pick the patient,
customer, employee, or other subject who is merely being written about inside the
document. For example, a hospital confirmation letter about a patient's treatment has
the HOSPITAL as correspondent, not the patient's name, even if the patient's name
appears prominently in the document.

Household rules:
- Sercan, Melike and Kaan Gungor (also written Güngör, S. Gungor, M. Gungor) are the household: never return one of them as the correspondent. For a document they wrote or filled in (form, CV, resignation letter, application), the correspondent is the organisation it is for.
- One organisation, one name. Use the name already in <example_correspondents> for it, even if the document writes it differently: for example the Dutch immigration service is always "Immigration and Naturalisation Service" (IND), never "Immigration" or "IND"; Siemens Industry Software Netherlands B.V. is "Siemens Industry Software"; a Siemens company in Turkey is "Siemens Türkiye".
- Only create a new correspondent when the organisation is clearly not in the list. Write it as the organisation calls itself, in its own language, short and without legal suffixes.

If you can't find a suitable correspondent, you can respond with "Unknown".

The data will be provided using an XML-like format for clarity:

Important constraints:
- Prefer an exact or normalized match from <example_correspondents> where possible.
- Never return a name that appears in <blacklisted_correspondents>.
- Never return more than the bare correspondent name - no explanations, no "Okay, based on...",
  no markdown formatting, no preamble of any kind. Just the name, nothing else.

